{
  "name": "frosted-glass",
  "version": "1.0",
  "author": "yodabytz",
  "description": "Frostglass \u2014 translucent panels for compositor blur. Backgrounds are low-alpha; text + krells stay fully opaque so nothing looks blurred but the surfaces themselves.",
  "comment_compositor": "For the frosted look you need a compositor that blurs translucent windows. KWin: System Settings -> Window Management -> Window Rules -> add a rule matching window class 'krellix' with 'Force Blur Behind = Yes'. picom (X11): add 'blur-background = true' and a 'blur-background-include' rule for the krellix window. Hyprland: decoration { blur { enabled = true; size = 8; passes = 2; }; xray = false; } and 'blurls = krellix'. Without compositor blur the panels just look transparent \u2014 text + krell + chart trace remain crisp either way.",
  "comment_alpha": "Every translucent value uses 8-digit hex (#RRGGBBAA). 30 = ~19% opacity for very subtle frosted overlay; 50 = 31% for a more present surface; cc = 80% nearly opaque for the chart canvas so trace lines read clearly. Increase the alpha values everywhere if your background is busy and the panels disappear into it.",
